  "slug": "graph-predicting-38af",
  "summary": "Recent work fuses protein language model embeddings, predicted structures, and graph learning across enzyme, PPI, and effector prediction tasks.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is representing biomolecular entities through structural or relational graphs and fusing them with complementary modalities. DMG-PPI applies a dual-channel graph neural network to separate similarity and complementarity in protein-protein interaction networks. GeoEPred combines pretrained protein language model embeddings with ESMFold-predicted geometric structure via contrastive cross-modal alignment, and GERO fuses enzyme sequence, pocket geometry, and reaction representations for condition-aware retrieval. TIGER pursues bidirectional enzyme-reaction retrieval using protein-to-text distillation and gated fusion. MetaESI applies interpretable meta-learning to E3-substrate binding interfaces, and TACK provides a curated PROTAC dataset with scaffold-based benchmarking of DC50, Dmax, and activity prediction. The novelty lies mainly in task-specific multimodal architectures rather than a shared method, and the items differ considerably in data modality and are not all graph-based.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-05-25"
}
